---
description: Golden tests are sacred; do not rewrite them to hide failures
alwaysApply: true
---

# Tests are sacred

- Write or extend tests before large refactors. Regression tests are the seatbelt.
- Never edit golden/vault fixtures or weaken assertions just to make a broken change green.
- Rewriting goldens requires an explicit `ALLOW_GOLDEN_UPDATE=1` (or user instruction). Default is deny.
- Prefer contract tests on host / ACP / A2A / discover over snapshot spam.
- If tests fail after your change, fix the implementation first unless the test is proven wrong.
